=== plan: the instruction at a FIXED token count, only BLOCK_SIZE_M moving ===
  model deepseek-v3   tokens 256   env vllm
  pinned across every arm: BLOCK_SIZE_N=64 BLOCK_SIZE_K=64
                           GROUP_SIZE_M=1 num_warps=4 num_stages=3
  forced through MOE_FORCE_TILE, and each arm's OBSERVED tile columns are
  read back out of its own run CSV before its PTX is censused.

  PREDICTIONS, registered before the run. Triton emits wgmma only when
  BLOCK_M % 64 == 0 AND num_warps % 4 == 0; num_warps is pinned at
  4 in every arm, so only the first term can move:
    BLOCK_SIZE_M=16   wgmma == 0   (16 % 64 != 0, so mma.sync)
    BLOCK_SIZE_M=64   wgmma  > 0   (64 % 64 == 0)

  GATES
    G1 VALIDITY  every arm's OBSERVED six tile columns equal the forced ones
    G2 VALIDITY  every arm dumped at least one PTX carrying a tensor-core instruction
    G3 VALIDITY  the arms compiled DIFFERENT kernels (distinct PTX checksums)
    G4 CLAIM     wgmma is present in exactly the arms the predicate names
  A G1-G3 FAIL means no census on the page may be attributed to a tile,
  and the run exits 3 INVALID: measured, unquotable, and NOT re-run.
  A G4 FAIL is a result: the instruction is not selected by the tile alone,
  and the run exits 1 CLAIM_FAIL, which the session records as finished.
  Each of the four prints one RESULT: line, which is all the driver reads.
  dumps to /workspace/session/gaps-nvidia_h200-20260909T031848Z/ptx/mma-switch/bm<N>/

